    <!-- The ONE failed-download line, on the picker's rows AND the offline
         manager's (#175, #130 PR-18). It replaced text_lang_error_* and
         offline_error_*, which said the same three things in two voices: one
         dropped connection read "No connection. Reconnect and try again." in the
         picker and "Download failed — check your connection, then retry" in
         Settings, which invites the reading that they are two faults. The
         surviving wording is the picker's on all three, because each of its
         sentences states the fact and then the way out; the retired set's
         "Something went wrong" states neither. Owned by DownloadFailure.kt. -->
    <string name="lang_pack_error_network">No connection. Reconnect and try again.</string>
    <string name="lang_pack_error_storage">Not enough space. Free some up and try again.</string>
    <string name="lang_pack_error_generic">Download didn\'t finish. Try again.</string>
    <!-- Sheet 19d — the download the user just asked for stopped. The title
         names the language; the body and the cause line are per cause, because
         the drawn frame is written for a dropped connection and ML Kit does not
         explain its other failures. "nothing is on the device yet" is the drawn
         copy and it ships as drawn: the frame's own caption claims progress is
         kept, and DESIGNER-BRIEF.md:73 forbids that claim — there is no resume,
         and Retry starts a fresh download. -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_title">%1$s did not download</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_body_network">The connection dropped before the pack was ready, so nothing is on the device yet.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_cause_network">Cause: connection lost. Retrying starts the download again.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_body_generic">The download stopped before the pack was ready, so nothing is on the device yet.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_cause_generic">Cause: not reported. Retrying starts the download again.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_close">Close</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_failed_retry">Retry</string>
    <!-- Sheet 19b — the download was refused before it started, because the disk
         cannot hold a pack (the 150 MB pre-flight in RealOfflineModelManager).
         The bar is used-against-free on ONE volume and never packs-against-
         device: at 110 MB the library cannot be plotted against a whole device
         without misstating one of the two figures (spec rev 5). The drawn second
         action, "Free up space", opens 20e, which is PR-25 — omitted rather than
         wired to nothing, per the rev3 ruling. -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_title">Not enough space</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_body">There is %1$s free on this device. A language pack usually needs 20–45 MB.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_used">Other apps and system</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_free">%1$s free</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_space_manage">Manage packs</string>
    <!-- Sheet 19a — the ONE mobile-data consent copy (#130 PR-17). It replaced
         text_lang_data_dialog_* and offline_data_dialog_*, two identical sets
         behind two dialogs. No language name: an answer here can be made
         standing by the checkbox, so a title naming one language would
         misdescribe it (spec rev 5 draws it that way for the same reason).
         "Not now", not the drawn "Wait for Wi-Fi": nothing in this app queues a
         download for Wi-Fi, experiment E-W1 has never been run, and the ruling's
         REJECT §7.8 refuses that word until it is. -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_data_title">Download over mobile data?</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_data_body">A language pack is usually 20–45 MB. Your plan may charge for it.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_data_always_ask">Always ask before using mobile data</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_data_download">Download now</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_data_not_now">Not now</string>
    <!-- Sheets 19f + 19g — the remove-pack confirm (#130 PR-19). The 🗑 on the
         offline manager used to delete on the tap; it now asks.

         19f ships EXACTLY as drawn, and every word of it is true of this app:
         removing a pack takes away offline capability and nothing else, so the
         language keeps translating through the AUTO waterfall's online tiers
         (RealTranslator.waterfall — ML Kit, then GOT, then GCT).

         19g does NOT ship as drawn, and the two edits are the point of this PR.
         The export draws "It is your target language. Removing it switches the
         target to English." Nothing switches: the language selection has four
         production writers (LanguagePickerViewModel.select and TextViewModel's
         three setLanguagePair calls) and the remove path is none of them — the
         model manager holds a ModelStore and a StorageProbe and cannot reach a
         preference at all. That also makes rev3 ruling 3 (owner-approved: the
         device language if catalog-capable, else `en`) an answer to a question
         the app never asks, so no fallback is implemented.
         The export also draws "They stay saved and will need a connection to
         reopen." Reopening a saved phrase needs neither connection nor pack —
         TextViewModel.onHistoryPick shows the STORED answer without calling an
         engine. Both sentences say what actually happens instead.

         The saved line is a plural so one phrase does not read "1 saved
         phrases", and it is drawn only when the count is above zero: an absent
         line, never a sentence about nothing. -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_title">Remove %1$s?</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_body">Frees space on this device. %1$s will need a connection to translate until you download it again.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_confirm">Remove</string>
    <!-- Shared by both sheets: one word, one key (the #175 stance on duplicated copy). -->
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_cancel">Cancel</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_inuse_title">%1$s is in use right now</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_inuse_body">It is your target language, and it stays your target. Translations into %1$s will need a connection until you download it again.</string>
    <string name="lang_sheet_remove_inuse_confirm">Remove anyway</string>
    <plurals name="lang_sheet_remove_inuse_saved">
        <item quantity="one">%1$d saved phrase uses %2$s. It stays saved and still opens without a connection.</item>
        <item quantity="other">%1$d saved phrases use %2$s. They stay saved and still open without a connection.</item>
    </plurals>
    <!-- The real catalog size, never the design's hardcoded 65 (plan §4). -->
    <plurals name="text_lang_search_hint">
        <item quantity="one">Search %1$d language</item>
        <item quantity="other">Search %1$d languages</item>
    </plurals>
    <!-- Denominator = offline-CAPABLE languages (59), not the 194-row catalog:
         "12 of 194 on device" would imply the other 182 are downloadable. -->
    <plurals name="text_lang_on_device_count">
        <item quantity="one">%1$d of %2$d on device</item>
        <item quantity="other">%1$d of %2$d on device</item>
    </plurals>
    <!-- Offline-library meter, foldable two-leaf (17b / U-5). The big numeral is
         its own key so locales with their own digits shape it; the line beside it
         carries the denominator (offline-CAPABLE, as above) and the size.
         THREE detail lines, not one with a blank: each says something the app has
         actually established. `_used` needs a measured walk of ML Kit's model
         store. `_free` is what it says when that walk cannot answer, because
         "0 MB used" would be a claim about the disk that nothing checked — and
         that is not a rare state: a pm clear on emulator-5554 drew
         "1 of 59 packs · 8.6 GB free" on the very first frame, since ML Kit counts
         the English pivot before anything is downloaded (E-S1b). `_none` outranks
         both whenever the count is zero, because a size under a count of nought
         is a size for something the user does not have. -->
    <string name="text_lang_library_title">Offline library</string>
    <string name="text_lang_library_downloaded">%1$d</string>
    <plurals name="text_lang_library_used">
        <item quantity="one">of %1$d pack · %2$s used</item>
        <item quantity="other">of %1$d packs · %2$s used</item>
    </plurals>
    <plurals name="text_lang_library_free">
        <item quantity="one">of %1$d pack · %2$s free</item>
        <item quantity="other">of %1$d packs · %2$s free</item>
    </plurals>
    <plurals name="text_lang_library_none">
        <item quantity="one">of %1$d pack · nothing downloaded</item>
        <item quantity="other">of %1$d packs · nothing downloaded</item>
    </plurals>
